entry.summary:
I built a Screenshot/PDF API that does more than just screenshots. The metadata endpoint extracts 50+ fields from any URL — OG tags, Twitter Card, JSON-LD, content analysis, and more. URL to Screenshot — capture any webpage as PNG, JPEG, or WebP URL to PDF — generate PDFs with custom format, margins, orientation Metadata Extraction — 50+ fields from any URL (see below) HTML to Image — render custom HTML/CSS to PNG/JPEG/WebP This is what makes it different. A single GET request extracts: Basic SEO: Open Graph: Twitter Card: @site, @creator Icons & Theme: Content Analysis: Structured Data: Feeds: Raw dump: import requests
headers = { "X-RapidAPI-Key": "YOUR_KEY", "X-RapidAPI-Host": "screenshot-pdf-api.p.rapidapi.com" }
